{"claims":[{"excerpt":"Uitgevouwen was Webb nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap","claim":"Webb was deployed before it was ready for routine science.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings. This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes reaching the fully deployed configuration in the second week from beginning routine science after commissioning.","materiality":"Central to the piece."},{"excerpt":"De James Webb-ruimtetelescoop moest opgevouwen in de kuip van de Ariane 5-raket passen, omdat zijn operationele configuratie te groot was om daarin te passen.","claim":"Webb had to fit folded inside the Ariane 5 fairing because its operational configuration was too large to fit there.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's fully deployed operational configuration is far too large to fit into any available rocket so it was designed to fold into a compact launch configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","narrative":"Webb moest compact in de Ariane 5-raket passen, hoewel zijn operationele configuratie daarvoor te groot was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This accurately summarizes the reason for the folded launch configuration.","materiality":"Provides relevant design context."},{"excerpt":"Het uitvouwen omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"Webb’s deployment involved many steps and possible points of failure.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source gives specific counts supporting this summary.","materiality":"Conveys the complexity and stakes of deployment."},{"excerpt":"Die risicovolle fase verliep soepel.","claim":"The risky deployment phase proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly describes the deployment as remarkably smooth.","materiality":"Clarifies that the cited risks did not mean deployment went wrong."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld, en had Webb zijn operationele configuratie bereikt.","claim":"By the second week, Webb’s mirror structures had unfolded and latched, bringing it to its fully deployed operational configuration.","category":"chronology","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings. This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld en had Webb zijn operationele configuratie bereikt.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source says the secondary-mirror tripod and primary-mirror wings were unfolded and latched, rather than describing the mirror surfaces themselves as unfolding. This is understandable shorthand for the deployed mirror structures.","materiality":"Minor technical imprecision; the timing and milestone are accurate."},{"excerpt":"Dat was een belangrijke mijlpaal, maar niet het einde van de ingebruikname.","claim":"Reaching the operational configuration was an important milestone, but commissioning was not yet complete.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.","narrative":"een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes substantial commissioning work after deployment.","materiality":"Expresses the piece’s central distinction."},{"excerpt":"De telescoop moest nog weken afkoelen","claim":"The telescope still needed several weeks to cool down after deployment.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The telescope and scientific instruments started to cool rapidly in the shade of the sunshield, but it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures.","narrative":"weken van afkoeling","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source says the telescope and instruments took several weeks to reach stable temperatures.","materiality":"Describes a significant commissioning task."},{"excerpt":"waarna de spiegeluitlijning maanden in beslag nam.","claim":"Mirror alignment took months after the cooldown.","category":"chronology","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"In the second, third and fourth months: Initial optics checkouts, and telescope alignment. ... Cooldown effectively ended and the cryocooler started running at its lowest temperature","narrative":"afkoeling, spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden.","narrativeRelation":"differs","origin":"independently_introduced","explanation":"Alignment did take place over months, but the wording “waarna” suggests cooling was complete before alignment began. The source places alignment in months two through four and says cooldown effectively ended during that period, so the phases partly overlapped.","materiality":"Minor chronology compression; it does not change the main distinction between deployment and commissioning."},{"excerpt":"Ook werden de instrumenten gekalibreerd.","claim":"Webb’s scientific instruments were calibrated during commissioning.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"In the fifth and sixth months: Calibration and completion of commissioning. We meticulously calibrated all of the scientific instruments’ many modes of operation","narrative":"instrumentkalibratie","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly reports calibration of the scientific instruments during months five and six.","materiality":"One of the tasks that followed deployment."},{"excerpt":"Pas na zes maanden ingebruikname begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science only after six months of commissioning.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This matches the source’s stated endpoint of commissioning and start of routine science operations.","materiality":"Establishes the timeline’s endpoint."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing was dus voltooid voordat de telescoop klaar was voor die fase.","claim":"Deployment was completed before Webb was ready for routine science.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places full deployment in the second week and routine science operations after six months.","materiality":"Summarizes the main timing relationship."}]}

